ORIGIN OF THE CODE - READ THIS BEFORE REDISTRIBUTING
================================================================================

This project is a PORT. Its core, src/unlock_v2.c, is derived from other
unlock projects and research. The details matter for licensing, so they are
stated explicitly rather than left for a reader to discover.


1. WildFlash1st/cmp90hx-unlock-for-windows  (PRIMARY UPSTREAM)
   https://github.com/WildFlash1st/cmp90hx-unlock-for-windows

   src/unlock_v2.c originated here as the CMP 90HX (GA102) unlock and was ported
   to the CMP 70HX (GA104) in this tree. The port note at the top of the file
   names the upstream explicitly.

   LICENSE STATUS: upstream carries NO license. Absent an explicit grant, its
   code is "all rights reserved" by default. This is the single most important
   fact in this file. We did not receive a written permission to redistribute
   it. It is published here in the belief that the work was put up publicly for
   the community to build on, but that belief is not a license, and no warranty
   of legal standing is given here.

   If you are the author of that project and want this to stop, say so and it
   will come down.


2. bendy2/cmp90hx
   https://github.com/bendy2/cmp90hx

   Source of the V67 canary exploit research and the direct-compute patch for
   driver 580.159.03 that opened PLM on the 90HX. That research is what the
   unlock protocol in this tree actually does.

   LICENSE STATUS: also NO license. Same problem as (1).


3. Jon Pry, "A Canary in the Crypto Mine: Defeating Stack Protection in a GPU
   Secure Coprocessor" (Zenodo, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20916112)

   The stack-canary overflow in the SEC2 booter that the V67 payload exploits is
   documented by this paper. It is a research result, cited, not copied.
   Quoted material is attributed at the point of use.


4. jdowning100/cmpunlocker  (GPL-2.0)
   https://github.com/jdowning100/cmpunlocker

   Source of the rejoin16 method (PLM / render masks) and the PCIe Gen2
   register work, ported into this project. This one IS GPL-2.0, which is
   consistent with this project being GPL-2.0.

   LICENSE STATUS: GPL-2.0. Ported, not copied wholesale; the derived routines
   in src/unlock_v2.c carry this project's own commentary.


5. xrip/cmp50hx-unlock  (MIT per its own README)
   https://github.com/xrip/cmp50hx-unlock

   Primary inspiration. A translated excerpt of its Windows README is kept under
   vendor/ with attribution; it documents the CMP 50HX (GA107), not the 70HX.
   Nothing from it is required to build this project.

   LICENSE STATUS: vendor/README.md records MIT. GitHub's API reports
   NOASSERTION, so the LICENSE file in that repo should be treated as the
   authoritative statement.


6. d3dx9 - Falcon emulator and ROP chain, referenced in the research notes.
   Cited as prior work.


================================================================================
NOT DISTRIBUTED HERE
================================================================================

The following are NOT in this repository and must not be added to it. They are
signed NVIDIA firmware or exploit payloads; see .gitignore and BUILDING.md 2.

  v67_payload.bin                    V67 exploit payload
  booter_ucode_prod_patched.bin       patched SEC2 booter, PROD
  booter_ucode_dbg_patched.bin       patched SEC2 booter, DBG
  gsp_rm_boot*.bin                   GSP boot blobs
  *.rom                              VBIOS images with NVIDIA FWSEC signatures
  *.efi, *.img                       built loader and flash image

The build links the blobs at the objcopy stage. Obtain them yourself; the
project tells you how in BUILDING.md.


